      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "$$g(a)=a=3a-4$$\n$$2a-4=0$$\n$$2a=4$$\n$$a=\\boxed{2}$$\n\nAlternatively, notice that $g(x)$ is linear.  Solving for $x$ immediately gives us $x=\\tfrac{4}{3}$.  Thus, the answer is $\\boxed{\\tfrac{4}{3}}$. To solve for the value of \\(a\\) in the equation \\(g(a) = 0\\) for the function \\(g(x) = 3x - 4\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\(a\\) into the function \\(g(x)\\) and set it equal to 0.\n2. Solve the resulting equation for \\(a\\).\n\nLet's solve it step-by-step:\n\n1. Start with the equation \\(g(a) = 0\\). Substituting the function \\(g(x) = 3x - 4\\), we get:\n\\[3a - 4 = 0\\]\n\n2. Solve the equation for \\(a\\):\n\\[3a - 4 = 0\\]\n\\[3a = 4\\]\n\\[a = \\frac{4}{3}\\]\n\nWe will verify this solution using Python code.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the variable\na = symbols('a')\n\n# Define the function g(x)\ng = 3 * a - 4\n\n# Set up the equation g(a) = 0\nequation = Eq(g, 0)\n\n# Solve the equation for a\nsolution = solve(equation, a)\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n[4/3]\n```\nThe solution to the equation \\(g(a) = 0\\) for the function \\(g(x) = 3x - 4\\) is indeed \\(a = \\frac{4}{3}\\).\n\nSo, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{4}{3}}\\).",
